<title>FRANCE: AGF says sale of Moroccan unit effective June 30.</title>
<headline>AGF says sale of Moroccan unit effective June 30.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Assurances Generales de France said on Tuesday that the sale of its 40 percent stake in Compagnie Africaine d'Assurances (CAA) to Morocco's private conglomerate ONA Group will be be effective on June 30 at the latest, with retroactive effect as of January 1 of this year.</p>
<p>In a statement AGF said the sale was in line with its selective development strategy abroad.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
